<title>GERMANY: Bilfinger wins 100 mln dmk Vietnam order.</title>
<headline>Bilfinger wins 100 mln dmk Vietnam order.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Bilfinger + Berger AG said on Tuesday it had won an order worth 100 million marks ($59 million) to build a bridge over the Mekong river in Vietnam.</p>
<p>Bilfinger said the order was won by its Australian unit Baulderstone Hornibrook Engineering. Construction will take 42 months.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.693 German Marks)</p>
